     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\">\r\n    <div>Le 03/11/2014 22:38, Irene T. Roca a\r\n      écrit :<br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    </div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\"><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n      <div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">Hello,</span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">I&#39;m\r\n            working\r\n            with the function “oscillo” in {seewave} and I’ll like to\r\n            know which are the\r\n            amplitude units that it’s using. When I write the\r\n            code: oscillo(a,\r\n            yaxt=&quot;l&quot;, xaxt=&quot;s&quot;) I get amplitude values in some cases\r\n            varying from -30000 to 30000. <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Thank\r\n            you\r\n            very much<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Irene<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"FR-CA\"> </span></p>\r\n      </div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\"><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n      -- <br>\r\n      You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google\r\n      Groups &quot;seewave&quot; group.<br>\r\n      To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it,\r\n      send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">seewave+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n      For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472382701000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2CkyiieXKeTL7xWRf-pO1X\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n    </blockquote>\r\n    Hello,<br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    The oscillo() function does not have an y-axis unit as, as you\r\n    suggested, the input can vary on any range depending on the source\r\n    file format. The values are often not calibrated, ie no absolute\r\n    pressure (Pa) or electrical (mV) can be obtained. In most cases, it\r\n    is therefore better to think this axis as a relative amplitude scale\r\n    without unit.<br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    HTH<br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    Jerome<br>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
